# Repository & Documentation Standards

## Required Root Files
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | AI rules (this directory) |
| `README.md` | Overview, quick start, tech stack, env vars, scripts |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Coding standards, branching, commit convention, PR checklist |
| `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` | System design, ERD, module boundaries, transaction rules |
| `docs/WORKFLOW.md` | Business workflows: Attendance, Leave, Overtime, Approvals |
| `docs/ADR/` | Architecture Decision Records (ADR-0001-…, one per significant decision) |
| `.env.example` | Every required env var documented, no secrets |

When generating a new module, **also update** the relevant doc (`WORKFLOW.md` for a business flow, `ARCHITECTURE.md` for a structural change) — do not silently drift.

## Branching & Commits
- Branches: `feat/<scope>`, `fix/<scope>`, `chore/<scope>`, `refactor/<scope>`.
- Commits: **Conventional Commits** (`feat(leave): add carry-over rule`).
- No commits directly to `main` — always PR + review.

## PR Checklist (generated PRs must satisfy)
- [ ] DTOs / Zod schemas added or updated
- [ ] Prisma migration included (if schema changed) and reviewed
- [ ] Unit tests for new domain logic
- [ ] Audit log emitted for sensitive mutations
- [ ] Tenant / RBAC scoping verified
- [ ] Docs updated (`WORKFLOW.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md`) when behavior changes
- [ ] No `any`, no `TODO`, no leaked secrets, no `console.log`

## Environment
- `NODE_ENV`, `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `JWT_EXPIRES_IN`, `S3_*` (attachments), `APP_TIMEZONE` default `Asia/Jakarta`.
- Never commit `.env` — only `.env.example`.
